===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:acte|tree=1}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂eǵ-|id=drive}}
From {{inh|en|enm|acte}}, from {{der|en|fro|acte}}, from {{der|en|la|ācta||register of events}}, plural of {{m|la|āctum||decree, law}}, from {{m|la|ago|agere|to do, to act}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₂éǵeti}}. Compare {{cog|de|Akte||file}}. Partially displaced {{m|en|deed}}, from {{noncog|ang|dǣd||act, deed}}.

====Noun====
{{wikidata lexeme|L5388}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} Something done, a [[deed]].
#: {{co|en|an '''act''' of goodwill}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1798|author=w:William Wordsworth|title=Lines
|passage=That best portion of a good man's life, / His little, nameless, unremembered '''acts''' / Of kindness and of love.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|uncountable}} [[actuality|Actuality]].
#* {{RQ:Hooker Laws|passage=The seeds of plants are not at first in '''act''', but in possibility, what they afterward grow to be.}}
# {{lb|en|theology}} Something done once and for all, as distinguished from a [[work]].
# {{lb|en|law|countable}} A product of a [[legislative body]], a [[statute]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2012-03|author=William E. Carter; Merri Sue Carter| title=The British Longitude Act Reconsidered| volume=100| issue=2| page=87| magazine=w:American Scientist| url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/the-british-longitude-act-reconsidered| passage=But was it responsible governance to pass the Longitude '''Act''' without other efforts to protect British seamen? Or might it have been subterfuge—a disingenuous attempt to shift attention away from the realities of their life at sea.}}
# {{lb|en|law|countable}} (In the United States) A legislative proposal, a bill that has not yet become law.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021-02-04|author=Celine McNicholas; Margaret Poydock; Lynn Rhinehart| title=How the PRO Act restores workers' rights to unionize|  magazine=w:Economic Policy Institute| url=https://www.epi.org/publication/pro-act-problem-solution-chart/| passage=Under current law, employers can drag out the union election process... Under the PRO Act, workers and the NLRB set union election procedures. The employer is not involved.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260811011200/https://www.epi.org/publication/pro-act-problem-solution-chart/|archivedate=11 August 2026}}
# The process of doing something.
#: {{ux|en|He was caught in the '''act''' of stealing.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A formal or official record of something done.
# {{senseid|en|theatrical}} {{lb|en|countable|drama}} A division of a [[theatrical]] [[performance]].
#* {{RQ:Orczy Miss Elliott|chapter=The Lisson Grove Mystery|passage=“H'm !” he said, “so, so—it is a tragedy in a prologue and three '''acts'''. I am going down this afternoon to see the curtain fall for the third time on what {{...}} will prove a good burlesque ; but it all began dramatically enough. It was last Saturday {{...}} that two boys, playing in the little spinney just outside Wembley Park Station, came across three large parcels done up in American cloth. {{...}}”}}
#: {{ux|en|The pivotal moment in the play was in the first scene of the second '''act'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[performer]] or performers in a show.
#: {{ux|en|Which '''act''' did you prefer? The soloist or the band?}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} Any organized activity.
#* {{quote-book|en|title=One egg: a farce in one act|page=46|author=Babette Hughes|year=1934|passage=The minute you let it be known you're planning a sales campaign everybody wants to get into the '''act'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[display]] of [[behaviour]].
## {{lb|en|countable}} A display of behaviour meant to [[deceive]].
##: {{co|en|to put on an '''act'''}}
##* {{quote-song|en|author={{w|Tate McRae}}; {{w|Amy Allen (songwriter)|Amy Allen}}; Jasper Harris; {{w|Ryan Tedder}}|authorlabel=no|title={{w|Greedy (Tate McRae song)|Greedy}}|album={{w|Think Later}}|date=15 September 2023|artist={{w|Tate McRae}}|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8AtiHCDGZ8c|text=He said, "I'm just curious, is this for real or just an '''act'''? / Can't tell if you love or hate me, never met someone like that"}}
