=====Usage notes=====
*(''EU regulation:'') The European Union increasingly uses the term ''act'' in the [[short title]]s<ref>{{cite-journal|url=https://tlq.ilaw.cas.cz/index.php/tlq/article/view/581/579|title='ACTS' AND 'LAWS' OF THE EUROPEAN UNION: A STEP TOWARDS THE FEDERALISATION OF THE EU?|first=Magdaléna|last=Svobodová|journal=The Lawyer Quarterly|publisher=The Institute of the State and Law of the Czech Academy of Sciences|issn=1805-840X|page=53|year=2024|volume=14|issue=1|format=PDF|accessdate=2026-04-11}}</ref> of its largest regulations, despite the fact that the legally binding term for the legislative act is {{m|en|regulation}} (e.g. '''''Regulation''' (EU) 2024/1689 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 13 June 2024'' = ''Artificial Intelligence '''Act''''').

